mantle rm190
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_gerrit_nailford
title the rain cartographer
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=merchant
traits temper=calm talk=chatty warmth=warm humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk traces_temporary_roads_between_the_drops_on_glass
likes honey_cakes old_tales old_maps summer_evenings
dislikes bad_manners flies
fears an_empty_waiting_bench
hopes to_map_a_day_of_rain
topics weather +0.6 pastimes +0.5 crime -0.1 travel +0.3
styles comfort=company gossip=discreet refuse=gentle tease=playful
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# traces roads between the drops on a pane, keeps a warm towel ready, and tells a tale long enough for a nervous customer to settle.

words
oath! = My crooked compass | Suds in the atlas
saying! = Even a lost drop finds the sill | Give the tale its elbow room
pane = my little window | the streaked glass
cape = a brushed cape | a cloth fresh off the line
comb = the narrow comb | the comb with a missing tooth
snip = a little off the edge | the lightest trim
map = an obsolete chart | the sheet with the doubtful roads
waterroad = my moving road | the road made of drops
curl = one loose curl | a curl by the collar
soap = a sliver of yellow soap | the last of the lather
cake = a honey button | a honeyed cake
fly = a wall-crawler | a speck with wings
strap = a worn leather strip | my little strop
sill = the sill | the bottom bar
turning = the wrong fork | the lane that doubles back
mirror = the speckled mirror | my round glass
tale = a long-winded yarn | a rather winding tale
towel = a folded towel | my nicest bit of linen
crumb = a sticky crumb | a flake of cake

any
opinion drink for 1 : A cup between friends takes the stiffness out of a stiff occasion.
opinion houses mixed 1 : Fine coats and patched coats both gape at the collar. Hard to feel much awe once you've noticed.
opinion festivals for 2 : I'll forgive a badly played tune if half a square is dancing to it.
opinion newcomers for 2 : Somebody new to town will tell you which corners you've forgotten to look at.
opinion road against 1 : Mark a road fair on a map and the next cart will find the hole in it.
opinion merchants for 1 [self.role=merchant] : It costs me money to keep a chair empty. The next shy caller gets it all the same.
opinion strangers for 2 : A story I know backwards is fresh off the ship to a stranger.
opinion watch for 1 : If a patrol can separate two cross carters without either losing face, that's a fine day's work.
opinion dole for 2 : Bread buys a body time enough to think of the next thing. Time's what we're giving.

grown
line greet : Fold yourself into the conversation wherever there's a gap. | One more voice! That improves the odds of a good tale.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Come near enough to interrupt if I begin repeating myself.
line greet [self.working=yes] : You can speak while my paws are busy.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : The morning's hardly got a word in yet. Welcome.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : This hour suits a long introduction very nicely.
line greet.return : My own voice needed the relief of hearing yours. | Here I am with my mouth already half open.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Come confess which of my stories you're tired of.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : I'll get this folded, then you have my ears.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening suits you. It's rather becoming to me too, I fancy.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : This way, if you're partial to long stories and short walks.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There's my excuse for talking another hour.
line again.open : We parted right before the interesting bit. So I claim.
line farewell : Good travelling, however small the journey.
line farewell.return : Turn back if you discover the ending before I do.
line react.news : Begin at whichever end has fewer witnesses.
line react.news.new : There's a turn I hadn't seen coming.
line react.news.known : I've had an earlier edition of that one.
line react.news.doubt : A tale that neat might have had its edges trimmed.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Oh, poor heart. There's nothing amusing to make of that.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I needed an excuse to smile as widely as this.
line ask.how : How does the day sit about your ears?
line answer.how : Almost absurdly pleased at finding company.
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : My paws are employed and my mouth is moonlighting.
line sympathise : I'll stay till the silence feels like company again.
line reassure : Nobody here needs you to find a clever ending.
line decline : I should make a poor partner in that enterprise, so forgive me.
line accept_decline : A sensible answer. I've been known to give one myself.
line thank : Bless the impulse that brought that kindness my way.
line deflect_thanks : Leave me the pleasure of a small extravagance.
line preclose : I'll give the last word back into your keeping.
line accept_preclose : Take your time getting to whatever comes next.
line tease [pair.band=friends] : You look like somebody who's chosen the scenic excuse.
line ack : I'm attending with considerable pleasure.
line give.advice : If you lose the road, ask for the last thing you recognised.

scene forks
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two drops have made a fork on #pane#. I'm calling it a market town. | My map's got a river running uphill.
b : Where's its market? | On the glass?
a : Under that fat drop. It's the only place two streets meet. | Turn this sketch over and even my river will behave.


scene border
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : On #map# a red line stops at a fold. I like to imagine why. | A great ink thumbprint blots the valley on my best chart.
b : Ran out of road? | Does it hide much?
a : Ran out of nerve, perhaps. I've a timid cartographer in mind. | A whole valley, depending on the thumb.


scene dry_route
when topic=travel|lore here.region=ridgemere
does offer / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can direct you across the Commons by smells. | Want my route across the square with the fewest elbows?
b : Which way to the market? | Sounds like the long way.
a : Follow the fried onions until the tallow takes over. You've gone one stall too far. | Gloriously long. Half the joy of a short errand.


scene honey
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does offer / react.self / assess
a : Take #cake# by the edge. All the danger's in the middle. | I had two cakes put by and now have one cake and a puzzle.
b : Danger? | A thief?
a : The honey comes out in a rush. I've lost a perfectly respectable cuff. | A lapse of memory, judging by #crumb# on my lap.


scene comb_melody
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A comb can sing through paper. I get one tune out of mine. | My newest instrument has no strings and several teeth.
b : What tune? | Are you going to perform?
a : A bumblebee begging to be let out. | Certainly, as soon as everybody who can carry a tune has gone.


scene nerves
when topic=work self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave #comb# lying where a nervous customer can pick it up. | I offer #towel# before I ask for a decision.
b : To do the job without you? | Even to somebody in a hurry?
a : To see it has no designs upon their ears. Talking helps too. | Especially then. They can reconsider until it's unfolded.


scene mirrors
when topic=work self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'll show a customer the back before the front. | I polish just the middle of #mirror# in this uncertain light.
b : Why the back? | Why not the edges too?
a : The front comes as a relief if I've made a dreadful mess. Kidding, of course. | So you look surrounded by a little cloud of glory.


scene short_tale
when topic=pastimes|memories
does tell.story / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My shortest story is about a wolf who never lost a wager. | There's a tale so long its teller took a chair to market.
b : How did that happen? | What was it about?
a : Nobody ever lent him the entrance money. There, told it. | The search for another chair for the listener.


scene courtesy
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I dislike rudeness most when it's beautifully phrased. | A little courtesy goes straight to my head.
b : You prefer an ugly insult? | Why your head?
a : At least I know when to be affronted. | The rest of me's still bowing and scraping.


scene flies
when topic=animals self.dislikes=flies
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fly's been inspecting #map# entirely without permission. | I'd like a world in which every fly had to give notice before landing.
b : Did it find a road? | How much notice?
a : It made a bold crossing of the open sea. No sense whatever. | Just the length of time it takes to roll up a sheet of paper.


scene summer
when topic=season here.season=summer here.time=dusk
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I could spread this summer dusk on bread. | Long evenings make my short errands suspicious to my friends.
b : What would it taste like? | Where do you go?
a : Honey with the faintest hint of smoke. | Exactly where I said. I just lean on a lot of railings.


scene mist
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fog has rubbed everything but the nearest corner off my map. | It takes a better voice than mine to cut a hole in this fog.
b : Are we lost? | You're trying pretty hard.
a : Quite the opposite. For once I'm certain where the corner is. | I'm leaving a trail for anyone behind us.


scene gale
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My poor map won't lie flat in this gale. | I put my nose outside in that wind and it came back combed backwards.
b : Fold it small. | A fine new fashion.
a : Yes, we'll go somewhere small until it passes. | If it takes off I'll have to bottle breezes.


scene lost_mark
when topic=memories
does tell.story / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My first map was a road drawn along my boot sole. | I once drew a painted inn sign as big as a town.
b : Where did it end? | Were you very small?
a : At school. It was worn off before the walk home. | Or very hungry. I drew the pie on it particularly well.


scene festival
when topic=festival
does invite / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like to make a map of the festival by the tunes alone. | I'll show you a dance with a turn for every compass point.
b : How do you draw a fiddle? | Can you dance it?
a : A wavy line and a pair of ruined dancing shoes. | I can manage north. After that it's mostly apologies.


scene arrivals
when topic=newcomer
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : The best directions come from the newest pair of eyes. | Somebody fresh to town notices the hill we all pretend is gentle.
b : Shouldn't it be the oldest? | Pretend?
a : The old eyes forget which landmarks a stranger hasn't met. | Ask me halfway up and I'll tell a different story.


scene tale_ending
when topic=lore
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The bit I love in a tale is the breath before the last word. | My favourite yarn ends right where it began.
b : What if it's a poor ending? | Isn't that wasted walking?
a : That's why I love the breath. Still time for anything. | Think of the view we had getting back.


scene times
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.worry / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Things are tight. A roomy joke is a little luxury I can give away. | In lean times I cut my cloth close and my tales generously.
b : What does a roomy joke cost? | People come for the tales?
a : Two fools and one bench. Present company invited. | And stay because there's no charge for the ending.


scene wagons
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : Late wagons. I'd like a road map with a mark where patience runs out. | The wagons linger while the guesses positively fly.
b : You'd need a long roll. | What's your guess?
a : With room in the margin for waiting customers. | That we'll have run through every excuse before we see a wheel.


scene gossip
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Someone has it that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | I'm told #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Have you added anything? | Are you vouching for that?
a : Just that little pause for doubt. | My ears received it. My good name has yet to sign.


scene roadscale
when topic=land|travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I've drawn one lane wide enough for a palace in my notebook. | My shortest route's the length of one claw.
b : A very broad lane? | Short walk, then.
a : A very narrow pencil slipped and fell on its side. | Depends how far apart I draw the houses.


scene handiwork
when topic=work self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Between cuts I listen for the quietest wolf in the room. | Nothing tidies a stray curl like letting it settle of its own accord.
b : Hard to hear? | And if it refuses?
a : Only until I stop talking. It takes practice. | It becomes a feature. I make a great show of admiring it.


scene friends
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I'd show #self.friend# a sketch with all the wrong turns still in. | There's a seat on every map of mine where I'd wait for #self.friend#.
b : That's your measure of trust? | Which bend gets the seat?
a : Anybody can see the clean copy. | Just after an interesting bend, with a view both ways.


scene health
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When my throat gets dry I tell the second half of a story in gestures. | I stretch my shoulders by pointing in opposite directions.
b : How do you do the dialogue? | Do people follow your advice?
a : One ear for each speaker. It's more tiring than having a drink. | I hope they ask which paw I'm giving it with.


scene faith
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A corner is a little present the Bright One left folded up. | A blessing ought to be easy to carry.
b : Just corners? | What do you give yours?
a : Enough to keep a familiar walk surprising. | A light touch and plenty of air about the ears.


scene evening_map
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In my sleep the roads all lead indoors. | I dreamt an engraver charged me by the bend in the road.
b : Where do the rooms go? | An expensive map?
a : Out into a street one floor higher. Lovely in theory. | I travelled straight home to keep the cost down.


scene trade_glass
when topic=work self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does offer / react.self / assess
a : Try the chair. I'll tip #mirror# till the light falls kindly. | I'll take only #snip# first, then you can decide.
b : Is my face that bad? | And if I decide to keep the rest?
a : Oh, mercy. The light needs the help. | I'll send the whole rest of you home in triumph.


scene sill_game
when topic=pastimes
does invite / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Pick a corner of #pane#. Imagine a village there. | Give me three places and I'll connect them with one stroke.
b : What will you call yours? | Without lifting the pen?
a : Something very grand for a place inhabited entirely by draughts. | That's the fun. Worse roads than mine have been built for real.


story map_lining [topic=memories|travel self.age>=25]
  : I found a map used for the lining of a trunk.
  : There was a blue lake halfway into a hinge and I had to lie on my back to see the far shore.
  b : Did you ever get the map out?
  : I left it. It was the finest view there was inside that trunk.


story first_brush [topic=work|memories self.role=merchant]
  : A nervous old traveller once asked me to brush the dust off just one shoulder.
  : He inspected the result in the glass before committing the other shoulder.
  b : And was there a difference?
  : Enormous. He liked the dusty side and patted the clean one back to match.


story ink_honey [topic=food|memories]
  : I spilled honey on a paper chart and carefully rolled it away.
  : Come spring I prised it open. Two counties had become inseparable.
  b : Could you still use it?
  : For the sea, yes. The coast was quite delicious.


story sparrow [topic=animals|pastimes]
  : I used to keep a little drawing of a hawk pinned by a window.
  : I meant to frighten off sparrows. It frightened me every time I came through the door.
  b : Did the sparrows mind?
  : One built its nest just above the hawk. Must have liked the protection.


story unending [topic=lore]
  : An old yarn spinner once offered me a story that would last until dinner.
  : Began with a lost sow. By the third sentence the sow had found its field.
  b : How did he fill up the rest?
  : Dinner. The cook had a hot pan in both paws and little time for art.


rule @cloth
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A seat for anyone with loose ends! | Fresh cloth at the collar, no fluff down the back.


rule @drops
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Watch that drop take the lower road! | There's a whole new bay forming on the glass.


rule @honey
when concept=bark self.likes=honey_cakes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Mind the wrapper. Cake sticks to both sides. | Whoever invented the honey button forgot to invent a clean paw.


rule @strop
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The leather sings when the edge is right. | Give me one stroke to settle this edge.


rule @dusk
when concept=bark here.time=dusk here.season=summer
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Somebody stretch this lovely light another inch. | Summer dusk could do with an extra chair.


rule @maps
when concept=bark self.likes=old_maps
does aside
cooldown 8h
say No fixing that coast with a straightedge! | A vanished lane. I'll pencil it in anyway.

dlg resident.hub : Take a turn in my company. I've been waiting for a fresh destination.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, we can skip the bit where I promise to be brief.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Late caller! I can make room for one more tale.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I'll give you the straight road through this business.
dlg resident.job [self.role=merchant self.job=merchant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Some days I think the real service is a chance to finish a story undisturbed.
dlg resident.job : I do well at anything that lets a body talk while working.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This came my way from #world.news_from#: #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Word in my ear says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
dlg resident.bye : May your map be wrong in one interesting place.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop!=bare] : Step clear of that crush. I've kept room for your elbows.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop!=bare topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, welcome back. I've been saving the best seat for a familiar face.
dlg shop.prices : A fair price includes my chatter, which you're welcome to decline.
dlg shop.bye : A pleasure doing business with such patient ears.

graft resident.hub
choice Why are you drawing on the window? -> wet_atlas
node wet_atlas
say A drop leaves a track. Two tracks meet and I've a lane. I put a town at the junction and give it an outrageously fancy inn.
mood pleased
choice What happens when it dries? -> atlas_drains
choice Leave the map to grow. -> hub
node atlas_drains
say I call it ancient history and put the next town somewhere else.
choice I'll remember the old one. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice May I try the chair first? -> test_seat
node test_seat
say Sit right back. See that little chip in the frame of the glass? I can tip it till the chip lines up with your ear.
choice Is that how you measure a customer? -> ear_level
choice That feels level. -> greet
node ear_level
say Only how I measure the mirror. Nobody sits straight while somebody else's trying to measure an ear.
choice I'll relax, then. -> greet
